{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258237,"nonce":"wYG3euFMG7Y7u4Iapdgkvgl+jSg=","title":"drop_insert: a string boxed through zb_box_str is copied and freed instead of adopted","message":"`zb_box_str(v) { return zb_str_to_dynamic(v) }` (extern `$IO$string_to_dynamic`) is how the Lua and Python frontends box a Str. drop_insert's `boxes_string` recognised only the extern itself, so where the wrapper is not inlined (the interpreter body, sites outside loops) a fresh string whose last use is the box stays `call @zb_box_str(s); $IO$string_free(s)`: a copy and a free where `$IO$string_adopt_dynamic(s)` would take the buffer.\n\nSeen in the `-interp` HIR of a program appending `\"k\" + str(i)` to a list of objects (ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR).\n\nFix: ModuleFacts records functions that are exactly that wrapper (one parameter, one block, the copying box call on the parameter value, its result returned) and `boxes_string` accepts them.","files":null}]}